            "review_text": "Jarkko J\n13 contributions\n0\nNice quality for small money\nJan 2018 • Family\nWe ate here with (they have two restaurants in Quy Nhon) my family couple of times in our one week trip to Quy Nhon. Stuff has zero English skills, but what they have is good sense of humor, right attitude and super beautiful smiles. All of them were so polite and helpfull. Even the food was a bit of \"with Vietnamese twist\" we really could recommend this place. Also our kids ate like crazy every time. We tested several pizzas, spaghetti and salads. Especially salads were my personal favorite with just like 1,1€ (30k dongs) each, or even less. Pizzas from 1,8€ (50k dong, smallest full size pizza ever) up to 5€ for large (150k dong, still quite small, but enough). Basic spaghetti average 50k dong.\nRead more\nWritten January 19, 2018",
